{"videoId":"bAWPbbayGjc","title":"Fedora 45 Preview: The Changes That Actually Matter","author":"Linux Pulse Daily","authorId":"UCs8DUBiLIbdau-GTTtivjqw","published":1791144330000,"description":"What actually changes in Fedora 45? This English beta preview explains the practical impact of kmscon, RPM signature checks, debugging defaults, desktop secrets, Atomic installation, Stratis and developer tools. Includes examples and preparation advice.\n\nResearch snapshot: 2026-10-04. This is a beta preview, not a final-release review. Feature status and available images may change. The visuals are original explanatory graphics; they are not screen recordings or benchmark results. Narration uses a synthetic voice.\n\nCHAPTERS\n00:00 What actually changes?\n00:51 A better virtual console\n01:45 Packages need a trusted signature\n02:38 Debugging and safer defaults\n03:33 Desktop secrets move to oo7\n04:31 Atomic installation gets a new interface\n05:23 Install from another device\n06:19 Stratis becomes an installation option\n07:13 Python moves to 3.15\n08:12 A refreshed native toolchain\n09:08 Who should try the beta?\n\nOFFICIAL SOURCES\nFedora 45 Beta announcement: https://fedoramagazine.org/announcing-fedo...\nFedora 45 change tracking: https://fedoraproject.org/wiki/Releases/45...\nThe kmscon console change: https://fedoraproject.org/wiki/Changes/Use...\nRPM signature enforcement: https://fedoraproject.org/wiki/Changes/Enf...\nRestrict ptrace by default: https://fedoraproject.org/wiki/Changes/Res...\noo7 Secrets Service provider: https://fedoraproject.org/wiki/Changes/oo7...\nAtomic Desktop installer WebUI: https://fedoraproject.org/wiki/Changes/Ana...\nAtomic image-builder: https://fedoraproject.org/wiki/Changes/Bui...\nRemote installation for Atomic Desktops: https://fedoraproject.org/wiki/Changes/Web...\nStratis in Anaconda: https://fedoraproject.org/wiki/Changes/Str...\nPython 3.15 in Fedora: https://fedoraproject.org/wiki/Changes/Pyt...\nFedora 45 GNU toolchain: https://fedoraproject.org/wiki/Changes/GNU...\n\nWhich change affects your workflow most? Share your use case in the comments.\n\nIndependent educational commentary. Fedora is a trademark of Red Hat, Inc. This video is not affiliated with or endorsed by the Fedora Project or Red Hat.\n\n<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/fedora45\">#Fedora45</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/fedoralinux\">#fedoralinux</a>  <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/linux\">#linux</a>","viewCount":45,"lengthSeconds":600,"watchProgress":21.908914,"timeWatched":1792083229600,"isLive":false,"type":"video","_id":"5XtDVWgID0INXkGa","lastViewedPlaylistType":"","lastViewedPlaylistItemId":null}
{"videoId":"UO_msBFNv5M","title":"The Obscure Window Manager Project","author":"DistroTube","authorId":"UCVls1GmFKf6WlTraIb_IaJg","published":1517295118000,"description":"In this video, I discuss a new project I&apos;m thinking of starting--reviewing a dozen different window managers, some of them I know a little about, some of them I know nothing about.  I am also considering possibly uploading the virtual machine images to SourceForge so you guys can download them and import them into Virtualbox.  Would love some feedback on this!\n\nWindow managers I think I will cover:\nawesome\nfluxbox\nfvwm\nherbstluftwm\ni3-gaps\nicewm\njwm\nopenbox\npekwm\nqtile\nxorg-twm\nxmonad\n\n-----\n\nWANT TO SUPPORT THE CHANNEL?\n\nPlease like, share and subscribe. And check out my Patreon page:\nhttps://www.patreon.com/distrotube\n \nYour support is very much appreciated.  Thanks, guys!","viewCount":12642,"lengthSeconds":562,"watchProgress":62.890712,"timeWatched":1792063969500,"isLive":false,"type":"video","_id":"5gzBGBczLiWoHyqA","lastViewedPlaylistType":"","lastViewedPlaylistItemId":null}
