{"videoId":"7YIbpiyaSIA","title":"Day 488: santa cruises [bicycle nomad]","author":"The Loaded Pickle","authorId":"UCXHO8wBQzaKwgnewkG4BmhQ","published":1793046581000,"description":"all those kids packed up and left before me haha I think I move slow in the morning... I got a lot of good riding in until I ran into a marathon that was clogging the bike path. detoured around that and found the boardwalk (looked so fun) and kept riding until I reached the Whole Foods and no sign of my package. waited two hours and tossed in the towel, got some beers and rode to the camp. not my favorite camp ever. mac n cheese for dinner.","viewCount":7584,"lengthSeconds":2476,"watchProgress":14.564146,"timeWatched":1793116916343,"isLive":false,"type":"video","_id":"69634SOnwrcvS0Of","lastViewedPlaylistType":"","lastViewedPlaylistItemId":null}
{"videoId":"ilfhkmn09mE","title":"Noah's Ark \"100% Confirmed\"? What the 2026 Dig Really Found","author":"No Trace","authorId":"UCdiYQ01cr2E4HG3YX_Q8LFg","published":1791045702000,"description":"In September 2026, a team drilling into the Durupinar formation, a boat-shaped hill about 30 km south of Mount Ararat in eastern Turkey, set off headlines saying Noah&apos;s Ark had been &quot;100% confirmed.&quot; On September 26, Anadolu Agency reported no identified remains of a wooden vessel, and the excavation&apos;s head, archaeologist Cenker Atila, told the agency that headlines claiming the ark had been definitively discovered were misleading. On October 2, the governor of Agri, Onder Bozkurt, said there was no scientific certainty yet. Hundreds of soil samples are waiting on laboratory tests, no peer-reviewed publication of the 2026 findings had been reported as of October 2, and the project says a timeline for laboratory results will come by late spring 2027.\n\n🎧 Follow the No Trace History Podcast on Spotify: https://open.spotify.com/show/6Yy1rvfIz5BUljfQBoRFSv\n\nThis is the documented story, with claims kept separate from evidence: the 1959 aerial photograph and the 1960 expedition, the summit searches on Mount Ararat, Fernand Navarra&apos;s wood and its radiocarbon dates, the 1949 Air Force frame released by the Defense Intelligence Agency, the 2010 Hong Kong claim and the hoax allegation, Ron Wyatt&apos;s site, the geologists who explained the formation as natural rock and landslide structures, the 2026 radar and drilling season, and the flood stories that are older than Genesis.\n\nChapters:\n0:00 A Shape in a Photograph\n5:03 The Mountains of Ararat\n7:50 Wood in the Ice\n11:04 The Ararat Anomaly\n14:23 Ron Wyatt&apos;s Ark\n17:20 The Geologists Answer\n21:27 Soil, Radar and a Drill\n25:57 Older Than Genesis\n\nSources:\nAnadolu Agency fact-check (September 26, 2026) and statements by Agri governor Onder Bozkurt (October 2, 2026), as reported\nSivas Cumhuriyet University and Noah&apos;s Ark Scans statements on the 2026 field season; BakhtarRadar press release (October 1, 2026)\nCoverage by Anadolu Agency, Demiroren News Agency (DHA), TRT Haber, Turkiye Today, Daily Sabah, Fox News, Newsweek, The Jerusalem Post, the Daily Mail and Live Science, September-October 2026\nCollins and Fasold, Journal of Geoscience Education (1996); Avci (2007); Atabey (2025)\nLIFE magazine, September 5, 1960; Defense Intelligence Agency release (1995), as reported\nAndrew Snelling, Answers in Genesis\nBritish Museum, the Flood Tablet (K.3375) and Irving Finkel&apos;s Ark Before Noah tablet (2014)\n\nClaims by researchers, groups and press releases are presented as their claims. Nothing in this video is presented as proof that the Durupinar formation is, or is not, Noah&apos;s Ark; laboratory and radar results were still pending at the time of publishing.\n\nSome scenes are AI-generated reconstructions for illustration; archival photographs are shown where available. AI-generated scenes, including short AI-animated clips, are altered/synthetic content and do not show the real people, places or objects. Photo credits (Wikimedia Commons, CC BY-SA 4.0, cropped): The Durupinar site in July 2019, by Wikkiwooki; Durupinar formation photos by Zorka Sojka; British Museum Flood Tablet, by Mike Peel (www.mikepeel.net). License: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/ . The maps are our own graphics.\n\nNext case - Amelia Earhart and the 2026 lagoon search: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OEgsGJHtlV4\nPrevious case - the Chicago Tylenol murders, 1982: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=U2c-cWFNhZQ\n\nWhat would it take to convince you either way: a lab result, a peer-reviewed paper, or something else? Tell me in the comments.\n\nMore people who vanished without a trace:\nhttps://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLD5_Enp63v18\n\n<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/noahsark\">#NoahsArk</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/mountararat\">#MountArarat</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/durupinar\">#Durupinar</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/archaeology\">#Archaeology</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/notracehistory\">#NoTraceHistory</a>\n\nSubscribe for unsolved mysteries every week:\nhttps://www.youtube.com/channel/UCdiYQ01cr2E4HG3YX_Q8LFg","viewCount":7438,"lengthSeconds":1777,"watchProgress":13.720886,"timeWatched":1792091343393,"isLive":false,"type":"video","_id":"79QLYxFTljRsO23L","lastViewedPlaylistType":"","lastViewedPlaylistItemId":null}
