{"videoId":"33KbHV-dX8A","title":"Stop Struggling on openSUSE – Master Zypper Now!","author":"The Linux Lighthouse: Your Guide to Linux","authorId":"UCveCcreajE7Sewp0UzNzWgw","published":1755252005000,"description":"Zypper, openSUSE Leap, openSUSE Tumbleweed.\nWelcome to the ultimate guide to mastering Zypper, the powerful package manager for openSUSE Linux! In this video, we&apos;ll walk you through everything you need to know about managing software and system updates on openSUSE, including installing and removing programs, handling repositories, applying updates, security patches, and even performing full distribution upgrades.\n\n📌 What You&apos;ll Learn:\n\nWhat is Zypper and why it&apos;s essential for openSUSE users\nHow to install and remove software using Zypper\nSearching for packages and viewing detailed package info\nManaging repositories: adding, removing, and refreshing\nUnderstanding updates, patching, and full system upgrades (zypper update vs. zypper patch vs. zypper dup)\nAdvanced commands for efficient system management\nHandling package conflicts and dependency issues\nEssential tips and best practices to optimize your openSUSE system\n\nWhether you&apos;re a beginner or a seasoned Linux user, this video will provide you with practical, real-world examples and everything you need to make the most of Zypper on openSUSE. Stay updated, secure, and in control with this comprehensive guide.\n\n💡 Don&apos;t forget to subscribe for more openSUSE tutorials, tips, and tricks! If you found this video helpful, give it a thumbs up and share it with others in the Linux community.\n\n🔔 Hit the bell icon to never miss a new upload!\n\n🛒 Online Shop US - https://the-linux-lighthouse.myspreadshop.com/\n🛒 Online Shop EU - https://the-linux-lighthouse.myspreadshop.co.uk/\n☕️ Buy Me a coffee - https://buymeacoffee.com/thelinuxlighthouse\n☕️ Buy Me a coffee - https://ko-fi.com/thelinuxlighthouse\nhttps://discord.gg/bF54Fw9s3f\nGitHub - https://github.com/thelinuxlighthouse\nDiscord - https://discord.gg/bF54Fw9s3f\nMastodon - https://mastodon.social/@thelinuxlighthouse\n\n<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/opensuse\">#opensuse</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/opensuseleap\">#opensuseleap</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/opensusetumbleweed\">#opensusetumbleweed</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/leap\">#leap</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/tumbleweed\">#tumbleweed</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/microos\">#microos</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/slowroll\">#slowroll</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/leapmicro\">#leapmicro</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/suse\">#suse</a>  <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/sysadmin\">#sysadmin</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/linux\">#linux</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/zypper\">#Zypper</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/linuxtips\">#LinuxTips</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/linuxtutorial\">#LinuxTutorial</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/tumbleweed\">#Tumbleweed</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/leap\">#Leap</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/linuxcommands\">#LinuxCommands</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/packagemanager\">#PackageManager</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/linuxupdate\">#LinuxUpdate</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/linuxguide\">#LinuxGuide</a>","viewCount":4673,"lengthSeconds":394,"watchProgress":68.65077,"timeWatched":1793126209439,"isLive":false,"type":"video","_id":"BzgFf9Z7B2CFJJAp","lastViewedPlaylistType":"","lastViewedPlaylistItemId":null}
{"videoId":"eE9rf8pmTdk","title":"I Installed Linux on a \"GPU\"?!","author":"Spec Tech","authorId":"UCj8OaGS2GbkPe3HoiGhi3nQ","published":1793112794000,"description":"I Installed Linux on a Graphics Card?!\n\nThis $30 board looks like a GPU, but it has a laptop CPU, RAM, storage connectors, and USB ports. It turns out the IC847 PLUS was built to control a cryptocurrency mining rig. Now I want to see what it can do as a PC.\n\nI install Loc-OS, a lightweight Linux distro, on its SSD and put this graphics-card-shaped machine through everyday use. LibreWolf handles web browsing and 1080p YouTube, while LibreOffice and GIMP run smoothly. Then I set up Prism Launcher and try Minecraft 1.8.9—with results that surprised me.\n\nThere are a few bumps along the way: getting Bluetooth audio working takes some setup, and my attempt to upgrade the RAM from 4GB to 8GB leaves the machine unable to boot with the new stick.\n\nSo is Loc OS a good match for this unusual GPU-shaped PC? Watch the real tests and decide for yourself. If you’d like to see me build a proper case for it in part two, let me know in the comments!\n\n<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/gpu\">#GPU</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/weirdpc\">#WeirdPC</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/linux\">#Linux</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/locos\">#LocOS</a>","viewCount":7222,"lengthSeconds":635,"watchProgress":72.427144,"timeWatched":1793128886054,"isLive":false,"type":"video","_id":"EKbT0bCCPqHSU9dT","lastViewedPlaylistType":"","lastViewedPlaylistItemId":null}
{"videoId":"icboZ2eCW54","title":"I tried using Linux instead of Windows... and I didn't expect this","author":"JotaNova","authorId":"UC4bv_Gammz5ui9Fuyqz3L9Q","published":1792284303000,"description":"In this video, I try Linux Mint for the first time 🐧 and share my real-world experience: what I liked, what didn&apos;t convince me, and whether Linux is really worth it as an alternative to Windows. Is it as good as they say? Could it replace Windows for everyday use? Here&apos;s my honest opinion.\n\n📲 My social media\n\nInstagram: https://www.instagram.com/jotanova_/\n\nTikTok: https://www.tiktok.com/@jotanova_\n\n📩 Business inquiries and collaborations:\njnova.contacto@gmail.com\n\nIf you like technology, operating systems, comparisons, and real-world tests, subscribe to JotaNova for more content.\n\n<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/linux\">#Linux</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/linuxmint\">#LinuxMint</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/linuxmintcinnamon\">#LinuxMintCinnamon</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/linuxvswindows\">#LinuxVsWindows</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/windows\">#Windows</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/linuxforbeginners\">#LinuxForBeginners</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/trylinux\">#TryLinux</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/operatingsystems\">#OperatingSystems</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/technology\">#Technology</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/pc\">#PC</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/freesoftware\">#FreeSoftware</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/opensource\">#OpenSource</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/linux2026\">#Linux2026</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/jotanova\">#JotaNova</a>","viewCount":106174,"lengthSeconds":553,"watchProgress":13.92456,"timeWatched":1793129015255,"isLive":false,"type":"video","_id":"EgGJlQBIOJMjaMYJ","lastViewedPlaylistType":"","lastViewedPlaylistItemId":null}
{"videoId":"b-5XOZpXZMg","title":"[mpv #1] mpv player basics walkthrough","author":"Linguistic Mind","authorId":"UCZ_2W3ilvrS-20rk1reNIZA","published":1615050031000,"description":"I learned about mpv player through its use in the movies2anki add-on, and after a while I started using it as my main video player as well. In this video I talk about setting up mpv player for convenient everyday use as well as about a few tweaks and features of this player useful for language learning.\n\n0:00 Intro\n2:12 mpv website; manual page\n3:40 Interface overview\n5:17 Configuration files\n7:31 Configuring mpv (starting with mpv.conf)\n12:21 Profiles\n31:59 movies2anki profile\n33:28 input-test profile\n39:07 input.conf\n43:20 sub-seek: Navigating between subtitle lines\n53:45 Scripts\n55:59 JavaScript bug on Windows\n57:16 Installing scripts\n59:00 autoload.lua\n1:01:49 Blackbox.js\n1:05:31 Colorbox.js\n1:06:45 My scripts\n1:07:17 osc-show-hide-hotkey.lua: Toggling the On Screen Controller\n1:08:16 copy-subtitle.lua: Copying current subtitle line to clipboard\n1:09:37 copy-time.lua, copy-time-in-seconds.lua: Copying current timecode to clipboard\n1:10:53 Outro\n\nmpv series playlist: https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLKLKspXiJeKaRA3fMi7bFcXm6BwMteINO\n\nmovies2anki tutorial (explains how to install mpv player): https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ilXT0fe-wpA\nmpv: http://mpv.io/\nmpv manual: https://mpv.io/manual/stable/\nAtom: http://atom.io/\nDefault input.conf: https://github.com/mpv-player/mpv/blob/master/etc/input.conf\nmpv user scripts: https://github.com/mpv-player/mpv/wiki/User-Scripts\nJavaScript bug on Windows: https://github.com/shinchiro/mpv-winbuild-cmake/issues/76\n\nMy scripts for mpv: https://github.com/linguisticmind/mpv-scripts\nMy mpv configs from this tutorial: https://gist.github.com/linguisticmind/3fc5582330a069ee366c21c39d2b2269 \n\n──────────\n\nNotes:\n\nI say that when using quit-watch-later command you can&apos;t see the list of saved states. I also note that the saved states are saved in ~/.config/mpv/watch_later directory, but that they are not human-readable.\nSee https://mpv.io/manual/stable/#files under &apos;~/.config/mpv/watch_later/&apos; for a way to enable the functionality which allows you to see which files&apos; playback states are saved in the watch_later directory.\n\n──────────\n\nSupport Linguistic Mind\n\nPatreon: https://patreon.com/linguisticmind\nKo-fi: https://ko-fi.com/linguisticmind\n​","viewCount":22190,"lengthSeconds":4329,"watchProgress":6.529464,"timeWatched":1791932864808,"isLive":false,"type":"video","_id":"G17FvLVYDRzJFcNS","lastViewedPlaylistType":"","lastViewedPlaylistItemId":null}
{"videoId":"N3VyQmgrJjk","title":"ESCAPE from LOS ANGELES","author":"American Hobo - Train Riding","authorId":"UCaXUDj54dIDRtPUEcXNuObA","published":1791669611000,"description":"‼️ DISCLAIMER ‼️\n\nEntertainment only! Do NOT attempt to duplicate what you see in this video. This activity could result in serious bodily harm or death. Do not try and recreate any of the scenes. A.H. does not encourage or endorse freight hopping. This video is an act of artistic expression. A.H. is not responsible for other people&apos;s action. Trespassing is illegal.\n\n•••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••\n❤️ PLEASE DO ME A FAVOR SO THAT THIS CHANNEL GETS RECOGNIZED BY THE ALGORITHM...\n\n1) SUBSCRIBE \n\n2) LIKE EVERY VIDEO EVEN IF YOU DON&apos;T \n\n3) SHARE MY VIDEOS WITH AS MANY PEOPLE THAT YOU CAN EVEN IF YOU DON&apos;T LIKE THE PERSON.\n\nTHIS ALLOWS ME TO KEEP ON MAKING VIDEOS. \n\n\n•••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••\n\n🔴 My Other Channel on YouTube - American Hobo 🔴\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/channel/UCAQ3zSCMTvKBqPtNLu_fjSA\n\n•••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••\n\n🟢 American Hobo on Rumble 🟢 \n\nhttps://rumble.com/c/c-7909332\n\n•••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••\n\n📌 Telegram Group;\nhttps://t.me/americanhobo2026\n\n•••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••\n\n💲 Donate 💲 Donate 💲 Donate 💲\n\n*PayPal \nhttps://www.paypal.com/donate/?business=2LS6KXBW39YBA&no_recurring=0&item_name=An+American+Hobo+traveling+the+world.&currency_code=USD\n\n*Cash App\nhttps://cash.app/$AmericanHobo123\n\n*Buy Me a Cup of Coffee \nhttps://www.buymeacoffee.com/kingmax738qt\n\n*Patreon\nhttps://www.patreon.com/AmericanHobo","viewCount":126429,"lengthSeconds":1530,"watchProgress":1530.401,"timeWatched":1792182063165,"isLive":false,"type":"video","_id":"GJcu9Odl0FXxERwB","lastViewedPlaylistType":"","lastViewedPlaylistItemId":null}
{"videoId":"xJbl1I0NAFY","title":"New to openSUSE? Do NOT skip these 5 tips!","author":"Gnu To Linux","authorId":"UC95zeRjDuxifm06s1BJeuZg","published":1786714196000,"description":"You&apos;ve just installed openSUSE Tumbleweed or Slowroll, now what? Here are the 5 things you need to sort out first to avoid problems down the line.\n\nIn this video:\n✅ Why you should update from the terminal, not the GUI applet\n✅ How to check Snapper is actually protecting you (your undo button)\n✅ Getting media codecs working properly with Packman\n✅ Setting up Flatpak and Flathub for extra software\n✅ Myrlyn: the one GUI tool that actually works properly for updates\n\nCOMMANDS USED IN THIS VIDEO\nsudo zypper dup\nsnapper list\nsudo snapper create --description &quot;clean install baseline&quot;\nsudo zypper ar -cfp 90 https://ftp.gwdg.de/pub/linux/misc/packman/suse/openSUSE_Tumbleweed/ packman\nsudo zypper dup --from packman --allow-vendor-change\nflatpak remote-add --if-not-exists flathub https://flathub.org/repo/flathub.flatpakrepo\nsudo zypper install myrlyn\n\nNew to Linux and thinking about openSUSE? This channel breaks down real, practical steps for beginners, no jargon, just what actually works.\n\nEverything is on my website: https://gnutolinux.com/\nthanks to https://www.youtube.com/@openSUSE  for the amazing work you do\n\n<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/opensuse\">#openSUSE</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/tumbleweed\">#Tumbleweed</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/linux\">#Linux</a>","viewCount":11256,"lengthSeconds":920,"watchProgress":315.680379,"timeWatched":1793121548345,"isLive":false,"type":"video","_id":"GwiKJJhl7ouC3wGH","lastViewedPlaylistType":"","lastViewedPlaylistItemId":null}
{"videoId":"b2qe3L4BX-Y","title":"Make your Rust Binaries TINY!","author":"Let's Get Rusty","authorId":"UCSp-OaMpsO8K0KkOqyBl7_w","published":1662469220000,"description":"Join our Rust Live Accelerator waitlist (free Rust Job-Ready Roadmap inside):\nhttps://letsgetrusty.com/join\n\nLet’s Get Rusty is the #1 Rust education &amp; career development platform for engineers who want real-world skills and results. We combine a structured curriculum, industry-grade projects, expert review and feedback, and our Rust recruiter network — to help you master Rust and get hired.\n\n· Today I&apos;m going over how to drastically reduce the size of your Rust binaries.\n\nMin-Sized-Rust Repo: https://github.com/johnthagen/min-sized-rust\nFREE Rust Cheat Sheet: https://letsgetrusty.com/cheatsheet\n\nChapters:\n0:00 Intro\n0:30 Axum Framework\n1:11 Strip Symbols From The Binary\n1:28 Optimization Level Option\n2:01 Link Time Optimization\n2:22 Codegen Units\n2:58 Reducing Binary Size Further\n3:26 More Tips\n3:35 Outro\n\n<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/rust\">#rust</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/programming\">#programming</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/tutorial\">#tutorial</a>","viewCount":39071,"lengthSeconds":237,"watchProgress":17.141393,"timeWatched":1792084368516,"isLive":false,"type":"video","_id":"H5t4A9H55MXBYNht","lastViewedPlaylistType":"","lastViewedPlaylistItemId":null}
