{"videoId":"w_LnZGB8ejU","title":"Louvre: Build A Wayland Compositor On Easy Mode","author":"Brodie Robertson","authorId":"UCld68syR8Wi-GY_n4CaoJGA","published":1701115224000,"description":"Most Wayland compositors if not built from scratch are built from a library like wlroots but this is notouriously complicated to work with, fear not a new project has come along to fill the gap. That being louvre a C++ library aiming to be far less complex\n\n==========Support The Channel==========\n► $100 Linode Credit: https://brodierobertson.xyz/linode\n► Patreon: https://brodierobertson.xyz/patreon\n► Paypal: https://brodierobertson.xyz/paypal\n► Liberapay: https://brodierobertson.xyz/liberapay\n► Amazon USA: https://brodierobertson.xyz/amazonusa\n\n==========Resources==========\nLouvre Repo: https://github.com/CuarzoSoftware/Louvre\nWriting A Wayland Compositor: https://www.reddit.com/r/linux/comments/wwsiaf/writing_a_wayland_compositor_is_much_harder_than/\nThoughts On Wlroots: http://inclem.net/2021/04/17/wayland/writing_a_wayland_compositor_with_wlroots/\nXDG Shell: https://wayland.app/protocols/xdg-shell\nXDG Decoration: https://wayland.app/protocols/xdg-decoration-unstable-v1\nPresentation Time: https://wayland.app/protocols/presentation-time\nLinux DMA BUF: https://wayland.app/protocols/linux-dmabuf-unstable-v1\nSession Lock: https://wayland.app/protocols/ext-session-lock-v1\nTearing Control: https://wayland.app/protocols/tearing-control-v1\nFractional Scale: https://wayland.app/protocols/fractional-scale-v1\n\n=========Video Platforms==========\n🎥 Odysee: https://brodierobertson.xyz/odysee\n🎥 Podcast: https://techovertea.xyz/youtube\n🎮 Gaming: https://brodierobertson.xyz/gaming\n\n==========Social Media==========\n🎤 Discord: https://brodierobertson.xyz/discord\n🎤 Matrix Space: https://brodierobertson.xyz/matrix\n🐦 Twitter: https://brodierobertson.xyz/twitter\n🌐 Mastodon: https://brodierobertson.xyz/mastodon\n🖥️ GitHub: https://brodierobertson.xyz/github\n\n==========Credits==========\n🎨 Channel Art:\nProfile Picture:\nhttps://www.instagram.com/supercozman_draws/\n\n<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/wayland\">#Wayland</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/linux\">#Linux</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/opensource\">#OpenSource</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/x11\">#X11</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/foss\">#FOSS</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/linuxdesktop\">#LinuxDesktop</a>\n\n🎵 Ending music\nTrack: Debris &amp; Jonth - Game Time [NCS Release]\nMusic provided by NoCopyrightSounds.\nWatch:  https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yDTvvOTie0w&pp=0gcJCR0AztywvtLA \nFree Download / Stream: http://ncs.io/GameTime\n\nDISCLOSURE: Wherever possible I use referral links, which means if you click one of the links in this video or description and make a purchase I may receive a small commission or other compensation.","viewCount":25122,"lengthSeconds":819,"watchProgress":42.465093,"timeWatched":1792065122811,"isLive":false,"type":"video","_id":"NbCHTMGa9MsfOcWk","lastViewedPlaylistType":"","lastViewedPlaylistItemId":null}
{"videoId":"WVg-UYa9Mok","title":"GNOME 51, Fedora 45 & Kernel 7.2.7: Why It Matters","author":"Ton Does Linux and More!","authorId":"UCUDdGb82Xsv4_LQprelLhqA","published":1790179201000,"description":"GNOME 51, Fedora 45 Beta, and Linux kernel 7.2.7 all arrived with different implications for Linux users this week. This roundup separates the supported desktop update, the beta you should test deliberately, and the stable-kernel maintenance path you should verify through your distribution.\n\nGNOME 51 brings workflow-facing changes to frame scheduling, screen capture, laptop settings, remote access, accessibility, Maps, Files, and Software. The important caution is its move away from legacy NVIDIA driver interfaces: the official release notes do not say every setup is affected, but older NVIDIA users should check their distribution guidance before upgrading.\n\nFedora Linux 45 Beta is a test target, not a general production recommendation. It changes the virtual-terminal path, requires valid package signatures by default, introduces an updated secret-management direction, refreshes toolchains, and expands Atomic, CoreOS, and installer workflows. The practical task is to validate the paths that matter to you before Fedora 45 final.\n\nLinux 7.2.7 is the operational story. The official stable-tree diff records 655 changed files, 9,914 insertions, and 5,496 deletions from 7.2.6. That does not establish one universal severity rating or a total CVE count. It does justify reviewing the vendor kernel package and changelog if you are already tracking the 7.2 series.\n\nChapters\n00:00 Three Layers of Linux Change\n01:00 GNOME 51: Desktop Workflow and Compatibility\n02:56 Fedora 45 Beta: Test the New Defaults\n05:54 Linux 7.2.7: Broad Stable Maintenance\n07:34 The Practical Decision Map\n08:03 Like, Subscribe, and Stay Informed\n\nResources\n\n•\nGNOME 51 release notes: https://release.gnome.org/51/\n\n•\nFedora Linux 45 Beta announcement: https://fedoramagazine.org/announcing-fedora-linux-45-beta/\n\n•\nFedora 45 Change Set: https://fedoraproject.org/wiki/Releases/45/ChangeSet\n\n•\nLinux 7.2.7 official changelog: https://cdn.kernel.org/pub/linux/kernel/v7.x/ChangeLog-7.2.7\n\n•\nLinux 7.2.7 stable-tree diff: https://git.kernel.org/stable/ds/v7.2.7/v7.2.6\n\nFollow Ton Does Linux and More!\n\n•\nWebsite: https://tondoeslinux.com/\n\n•\nSubscribe: https://tondoeslinux.com/subscribe\n\n•\nFacebook: https://facebook.com/tondoeslinux\n\n\n=======================================================\n&quot;Please like, comment, and subscribe to receive more videos of this kind.&quot;\nhttps://goo.gl/a9JwXB\n\nSubscribe to the weekly newsletter:\nhttps://tondoeslinux.com/subscribe\n\nUse VidIQ for your channel:\nhttps://vidiq.com/TonDoesLinux\n\nUse the best VPN:\nhttps://surfshark.club/friend/FN3Sduq4\n\nLearn Linux:\nhttps://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PL_dJuuPxFr8H2tjU0vwWa4OQk0joraoYl\n\nLearn Arch:\nhttps://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PL_dJuuPxFr8GXLBrgfIuqoIZYzEoifreM\n\nWebsite:\nwww.tondoeslinux.com\n\nLike my Facebook page:\nhttps://www.facebook.com/tondoeslinux\n\nSee me on Twitter\nhttps://twitter.com/tondoes\n\n<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/tondoeslinux\">#tondoeslinux</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/linuxtutorial\">#linuxtutorial</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/linux\">#linux</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/apple\">#apple</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/tech\">#tech</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/shorts\">#shorts</a>","viewCount":4885,"lengthSeconds":501,"watchProgress":36.57693,"timeWatched":1792083154879,"isLive":false,"type":"video","_id":"OeEOOsOBki0vQ8me","lastViewedPlaylistType":"","lastViewedPlaylistItemId":null}
{"videoId":"W7iTQdRwQYc","title":"Day 489: traffic sucks [bicycle nomad]","author":"The Loaded Pickle","authorId":"UCXHO8wBQzaKwgnewkG4BmhQ","published":1793133515000,"description":"surprisingly quiet night for how busy this place is. made my way to whole foods for my packages, installed the seatpost, then went to home Depot and found the square tube I needed. dealt with horrible drivers all day. not the best bike lane either. the campground was empty when I got there, saw a coyote, made some good ramen and jammed out to some tunes all night.","viewCount":1184,"lengthSeconds":1849,"watchProgress":0,"timeWatched":1793138513717,"isLive":false,"type":"video","_id":"PE32QEgsU6DofXu3","lastViewedPlaylistType":"","lastViewedPlaylistItemId":null}
{"videoId":"jQe6CQOIZts","title":"WE'RE COOKED! Creepy & Mysterious TikToks NO ONE Has Answers For","author":"UNREAL REALITY","authorId":"UC--ZWWjLSOfuiatUrdr8lSA","published":1792008026000,"description":"WE&apos;RE COOKED! CREEPY &amp; MYSTERIOUS TIKTOKS NO ONE HAS ANSWERS FOR | REACTION VIDEO\n\nIn today&apos;s video, we&apos;re reacting to some of the most mysterious, unsettling, and downright creepy videos currently going viral! From unexplained paranormal activity caught on camera to mysterious TikToks that no one can explain, these bone-chilling clips will definitely make you question reality!\n\nInside this video, we uncover:\n🍼 Creepy suburban mansion hiding an underground baby-hoarding ring\n🤖 Dystopian AI assistants secretly switching to encrypted code behind our backs\n🛸 The FCC&apos;s frantic attempt to ban LiDAR drone mapping\n☣️ Chernobyl&apos;s radioactive black fungus acting like a living symbiote\n🎖️ Obama handing out secret club badges disguised as civilian medals\n👁️ Kourtney Kardashian failing an Illuminati lie detector test on camera\nPLUS, SO MUCH MORE!!\n\nWhich clip creeped you out most? Comment below - if you dare! And don&apos;t forget to like, hype, share and subscribe for more weekly disturbing and mysterious videos just like this!\n\n<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/creepytiktoks\">#CreepyTikToks</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/disturbingtiktoks\">#DisturbingTikToks</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/mysteriousvideos\">#MysteriousVideos</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/mysterioustiktoks\">#MysteriousTikToks</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/viraltiktoks\">#ViralTikToks</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/scaryclips\">#ScaryClips</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/unexplained\">#Unexplained</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/unrealreality\">#UnrealReality</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/weirdtiktoks\">#WeirdTikToks</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/hiddentruths\">#HiddenTruths</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/questioneverything\">#QuestionEverything</a>\n\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/@UnrealReality_","viewCount":6353,"lengthSeconds":1914,"watchProgress":1913.581,"timeWatched":1792015741592,"isLive":false,"type":"video","_id":"PfeT3lLYKlh4sxZk","lastViewedPlaylistType":"","lastViewedPlaylistItemId":null}
{"videoId":"HPpL1VwHtBs","title":"What is Fedora Hummingbird Linux? | Fedora Podcast 062","author":"Fedora Project","authorId":"UCnIfca4LPFVn8-FjpPVc1ow","published":1792062023000,"description":"Red Hat announced Hummingbird at Summit back in May. Five months later there are Hummingbird containers in the wild, a spin of Fedora Linux built on the same principles, and a full Bluefin ISO built on top of it. Scott McCarty and Jorge Castro join Eric to sort out what actually got announced, what each piece is, and how much has changed since.\n\nWe get into why the industry suddenly cares about patching speed, the difference between risk based and compliance based security, what separates a container image from a bootable one, and what it takes to point an existing home lab at Hummingbird. Jorge explains how the first cut of Utah Raptor got built in a bar on a dare, and how 13 people turned that into a shippable Bluefin in 22 days.\n\nScott and Jorge both have an ask at the end: tell them what you would actually use this for.\n\n🔗 Episode Resources\n\nFedora Hummingbird on Fedora Discussion: https://discussion.fedoraproject.org/t/fedora-hummingbird-taking-the-hummingbird-model-to-the-full-operating-system/191184\nFedora Hummingbird on Fedora Forge: https://forge.fedoraproject.org/hummingbird\nRed Hat Hardened Images: https://images.redhat.com/\nChasing the holy grail, why Hummingbird aims for near zero CVEs: https://www.redhat.com/en/blog/chasing-holy-grail-why-red-hats-hummingbird-project-aims-near-zero-cves\nProject Bluefin: https://docs.projectbluefin.io/\nUtah, Bluefin built on Fedora Hummingbird: https://docs.projectbluefin.io/utah/\nFedora bootc documentation: https://docs.fedoraproject.org/en-US/bootc/\nRamaLama: https://github.com/containers/ramalama\ngoose: https://github.com/block/goose\nBackground on Claude Mythos: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Claude_Mythos\nScott McCarty: https://www.linkedin.com/in/fatherlinux/\n\n🔖 Chapters\n00:00 Nobody wants that conversation\n02:09 Scott McCarty, from Podman to Hummingbird\n03:53 Jorge Castro, Bluefin and bootc\n06:53 Back to Summit, what actually got announced\n10:07 The Mythos moment and the end of slow patching\n15:52 What this means if you just use Linux\n19:59 Utah Raptor, and 13 people in 22 days\n21:49 Home labs, local models and agents\n28:09 From UBI to Hummingbird, the recap\n30:05 Risk based versus compliance based patching\n40:25 What the project needs from you\n47:53 Wait, we are not done\n\n🎬 New to Fedora? Get Started Here: https://fedoraproject.org/\n🎙️ Follow the Fedora Podcast: https://podcast.fedoraproject.org/\n💬 Join the Conversation: https://matrix.to/#/<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/podcast\">#podcast</a>:fedoraproject.org\n🌐 Become Part of the Fedora community: https://docs.fedoraproject.org/en-US/project/join/\n📱 Connect with Eric &quot;the IT Guy&quot; Hendricks: https://linktr.ee/itguyeric\n📱 Connect with Noah Chelliah (Kernellinux): https://noahc.us/about\n\n<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/fedora\">#fedora</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/linux\">#linux</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/hummingbird\">#hummingbird</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/bootc\">#bootc</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/containers\">#containers</a>","viewCount":245,"lengthSeconds":2935,"watchProgress":26.174849,"timeWatched":1792083334811,"isLive":false,"type":"video","_id":"Q8SJbpw4NLxG5UC2","lastViewedPlaylistType":"","lastViewedPlaylistItemId":null}
