{"videoId":"J9sZC8UlX8o","title":"New radar scans stun Noah's Ark researchers | Unreported","author":"NewsNation","authorId":"UCCjG8NtOig0USdrT5D1FpxQ","published":1791230410000,"description":"Some stories make headlines. Others get ignored. On &quot;Unreported,&quot; Meagan Medick takes a deeper look at the unexplained through the eyes and experiences of you, the viewers. You send the mystery - we investigate. This week, Meagan gets a live update from Turkey, where researchers are drilling for what some believe is Noah&apos;s Ark. Meagan speaks with Andrew Jones, founder of Noah&apos;s Ark Scans, who has studied the site for decades, and Lauren Witzke, director of fundraising for the project.\n\nThey discuss new ground-penetrating radar results showing what researchers call &quot;organized structure&quot; below the surface instead of solid rock, a drill bit that shattered on an unidentified hard layer several meters down and the mysterious &quot;drogue stones&quot; found scattered near the site that may have anchored the Ark. &quot;I personally was studying this since I was in middle school. ... I believe it&apos;s the buried remains of Noah&apos;s Ark,&quot; Jones says.\n\nWatch Meagan&apos;s interview with Cassie Copperstone here: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Qko_UnZq-ZY\n\nFollow Meagan!\nhttps://x.com/Producer_Meagan\ninstagram.com/ProducerMeagan\ntiktok.com/ProducerMeagan\n\nNoah&apos;s Ark Scans: https://www.noahsarkscans.com/\n\n<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/noahsark\">#NoahsArk</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/researcher\">#researcher</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/mysteryanddiscovery\">#mysteryanddiscovery</a> \n\nCREDITS:\nHost: Meagan Medick\nExecutive Producer: Andy Gipson, Meagan Medick\nSegment Producer: Will Tomasi, Christine Jenkinson\nEditor: Kanyon Lyons\n\nNewsNation`s Unreported with Meagan Medick is built on the idea that some of the most important stories are the ones that don`t make the headlines. A seasoned network executive producer, Meagan brings a rare behind-the-scenes perspective to the front of the camera, taking the reins on stories she believes deserves more attention while asking questions other outlets often overlook or ridicule.\n\nThrough thoughtful conversations with creators, experts, and insiders, this show cuts through the noise to make complicated, viral, fringe or misunderstood topics actually make sense. Exploring stories ranging from government coverups to A.I. to paranormal phenomena, to explaining the origins of conspiracy theories and other enduring mysteries.\n\nNew episodes will premiere every Wednesday, offering bold perspectives on interesting stories that continue to spark widespread intrigue.\n\nNewsNation is your source for fact-based, unbiased news for all Americans. \nMore from NewsNation: https://www.newsnationnow.com/ \nGet our app: https://trib.al/TBXgYpp \nFind us on your screen: https://www.joinnn.com/\n\nCHAPTER SUMMARY:\n0:00 Intro\n1:15 Meet Andrew Jones &amp; Lauren Witzke\n2:00 First permitted study\n4:35 What is the Bakhtar radar scanner?\n7:20 What the scans reveal \n10:22 Was Noah’s Ark found?\n13:15 The drill that shattered\n17:08 What are drogue stones?\n21:16 26 stones found\n23:34 The village of 8\n24:40 Ancient maps mention of Noah’s Ark\n26:00 Crosses carved in stones\n27:07 Biblical comparisons\n33:21 The 3 big “ifs”\n36:08 Implications if this is Noah’s Ark\n37:16 What’s next for the researchers\n38:23 Lake Van theory\n41:45 Final thoughts","viewCount":469340,"lengthSeconds":2559,"watchProgress":107.264459,"timeWatched":1792091359658,"isLive":false,"type":"video","_id":"WA6vtDpD8gAUzviT","lastViewedPlaylistType":"","lastViewedPlaylistItemId":null}
{"videoId":"4G7ji1JDEfk","title":"Day 475: fun layover [bicycle nomad]","author":"The Loaded Pickle","authorId":"UCXHO8wBQzaKwgnewkG4BmhQ","published":1791931468000,"description":"decided to burn a day here and soak up the awesome views. found out I was low on water and cruised back into Tomales for 2 gallons. I let the camera go for the entire ride back, about 9 minutes of POV action! hiked around the area when I got back. took a cat nap and heard some crash happen right out on the road. couldn&apos;t see what was going on. beanie weanies and ramen for dinner!","viewCount":6992,"lengthSeconds":2049,"watchProgress":2038.38232,"timeWatched":1791996862032,"isLive":false,"type":"video","_id":"WiDp9ZGuVWIYAgiY","lastViewedPlaylistType":"","lastViewedPlaylistItemId":null}
{"videoId":"bbg6ztWecbU","title":"mpv: The Best Video Player for Language Learning","author":"Matt vs Japan","authorId":"UCpf4BknRWAjb_oYIHoMDGVg","published":1604253446000,"description":"The best way to learn Japanese: https://mvj.link/Zy76h\n\nMPV LINKS:\nmpv: https://mpv.io/\nmpv Manual: https://mpv.io/manual/master/\nmpv Script Library: https://github.com/mpv-player/mpv/wiki/User-Scripts\n\nConfig File Text: https://pastebin.com/MSKuV9xm\n\nMpvacious: https://github.com/Ajatt-Tools/mpvacious\n\nTexthooker: https://texthooker.com/\nClipboard Inserter (Chrome): https://chrome.google.com/webstore/detail/clipboard-inserter/deahejllghicakhplliloeheabddjajm\nClipboard Inserter (Firefox): https://addons.mozilla.org/ja/firefox/addon/clipboard-inserter/\n\nTIMESTAMPS:\n0:00 - Intro\n1:42 - Installation\n4:30 - Config \n7:13 - Basic Usage\n14:00 - Scripts\n20:31 - Outro \n\nMusic: Lo-Fi Bolero Perron","viewCount":187581,"lengthSeconds":1259,"watchProgress":0,"timeWatched":1791934465051,"isLive":false,"type":"video","_id":"Wwciy982To3Ji49f","lastViewedPlaylistType":"","lastViewedPlaylistItemId":null}
{"videoId":"j8KkQ3HmTIs","title":"The Easiest Way to Prepare Choco-Flan The Impossible Cake","author":"Ana Regalado","authorId":"UCVEFFaZFuxxp7yjBMWjta-w","published":1611254537000,"description":"Choco-Flan is aslo known as the impossible cake for a very good reason – the moist chocolate cake and creamy custard layers swap spots during baking. So if you are having a hard time deciding to make a chocolate cake or flan for dessert? Now you can have your flan and cake too!  \n\n1 box of your favorite store-bought chocolate cake \nPrepare as instructed on the box \n\nIngredients for the  flan:\n14 Oz Can Condensed Milk \n12 Oz Can Evaporated Milk \n5 Large or 6 Medium Eggs \n1 Tbs Vanilla \n4 Ounces of Room Temperature Cream Cheese\n\n1 Cup of Sugar for the Caramel \n\nUse the remainder 4 ounces of cream cheese to prepare flour tortillas \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AsBXk8QbrUY\n\nThank you so much for watching! Here are a few more recipe ideas! \n\nGuava Cheese Flan \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vjpRAc53hrg&pp=0gcJCR0AztywvtLA\n\nSweet Pineapple Tamales \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EWdOOq4OaNU\n\nOrange Flavored Mantecadas \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WCpL0EQeGJU\n\nRompope Tres Leches Cake \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=G2JBiClQri0\n\nMexican Sweet Bread Conchas \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Zsopf75kTTo\n\nEasy Mango NO-BAKE Cheesecake \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OKS9W_X-kkE\n\nMazapan Frappe \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=u4vj9keHb4E\n\nEggnog Pound Cake \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XcgCuvjunq8\n\n\nAguachile \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=t6Mp7yXLXTI\n\nSweet and Spicy Tamarind Kabobs \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Q-2izXp801I\n\nGorditas Stuffed with Chicharron \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5oqzej_OZU4\n\nCreamy Hatch Chile Pasta \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=S_jb3yAKWe0\n\nLoaded Beef Nachos \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gaICgFYdUfA\n\nDrunken Steak - Stovetop Recipe \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5P3ZLpxHEho\n\nShredded Beef Tacos \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SIIJopfSFSE\n\nAvocado Shrimp Salad \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lgpjDwH1iJM\n\nGorditas Stuffed with Chicharron \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5oqzej_OZU4\n\nTamarind Kabobs \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Q-2izXp801I\n\n\nPork with Chile Verde and Potatoes \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-75EWdPputw\n\nPotato Soup with Panela Cheese \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QtOaKymaM8U\n\nRed Pork Pozole \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MDIWwG4SsN0&pp=0gcJCR0AztywvtLA\n\nSopa de Fideo/Mexican Noodle Soup \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QI8XwxcLmMs&pp=0gcJCR0AztywvtLA\n\nCheesy Crispy Potato Rolled Tacos \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=12kHwUWTw84\n\nSweet Pineapple Tamales \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EWdOOq4OaNU\n\nTamales with Oaxaca Cheese and Poblano Peppers \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OvfGVidQaAc\n\nBeef Tamales in Red Chile \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EMzj9trWS1k\n\nPork Tamales in Green Hatch Chile Sauce \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DDVHRtWfH1g\n\nSweet Corn Tamales \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cqjwKKf_hVc\n\nTres Leches Cake with Rompope (Eggnog) \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=G2JBiClQri0\n\nPumpkin Spice Rice Pudding \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wM5gIA6dvUs&pp=0gcJCR0AztywvtLA\n\nMushroom Quesadillas \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=B722LFeE6ME&pp=0gcJCR0AztywvtLA​​\n\nCheese Entomatadas \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EbyG7M4jHc8&pp=0gcJCR0AztywvtLA​​\n\nHomemade Mazapan \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MY9POCqdZco​​\n\nChorizo and Beans Nachos \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8kTP7_FJ9vo​​\n\nFried Cheese Quesadillas\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qBZaBBNi0_I​​\n\nCheesy Potatoe Rolled Tacos \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=12kHwUWTw84&pp=0gcJCR0AztywvtLA​​\n\nHow to prepare the perfect red rice every time! \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1XXQoOQdt6U​​\n\nCreamy Chicken Enchiladas \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YdJO9BlKAK4​​\n\nFried Enchiladas \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qBZaBBNi0_I​​\n\nPotato Soup with Panela Cheese \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QtOaKymaM8U​​\n\nChilaquiles in Red Guajillo Sauce \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0KFx0nlYUJY​​\n\nHatch Chile Enchilada Sauce \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eMtYatOgSOo​​\n\nThe Secret to Making the Perfect Puffy Taco \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Vpl8GxMybzQ​​\n\nQuick and Easy Potato Tostadas\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gQmdo4VZu1Y​​\n\nFlour Tortillas Made with Cream Cheese \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AsBXk8QbrUY​​","viewCount":312300,"lengthSeconds":381,"watchProgress":290.757226,"timeWatched":1792024217805,"isLive":false,"type":"video","_id":"X2vENHUwPVJMY07v","lastViewedPlaylistType":"","lastViewedPlaylistItemId":null}
{"videoId":"2YibAiSQxwA","title":"If You See Me Use Ubuntu (Song Parody)","author":"DenshiVideo","authorId":"UCNwGa76xVVwdEVToRZBIUIg","published":1782281247000,"description":"UPDATE: An EXTENDED VERSION of this song is available on BANDCAMP: https://sabaudia.bandcamp.com/track/if-you-see-me-use-ubuntu-too-late-ive-already-deleted-windows\nAlso available on Tidal: https://tidal.com/album/538721204\n\nThis is a song parody of &quot;Nope Too Late I&apos;m Already Dead&quot; by Wifiskeleton, themed around Linux and online discourse.\n\nLyrics:\nI&apos;m not tryna ruin your fun,\nyou&apos;re just a little bit late,\nthe wipe&apos;s already been done\nand I couldn&apos;t use Gentoo\n&apos;cause I&apos;m too dumb\nmight shill openBSD\nit&apos;s really possible?\n\nIf you see use Ubuntu, I might say &quot;Hi&quot;,\nbut if you meet me running Arch, I&apos;m a talkative guy\nI&apos;ve been tryna fix my audio and solid state drive\nand I get a little closer every line I write\n\nAll these newgen Linux posers filling up my feed\nThey love proprietary software and KDE\nand the AUR maintainers&apos; tryna infect me\nGotta verify my age with systemD...\n\nNext day, I wanna play games\nbut what would Stallman think?\nThat it&apos;s no longer the same\nand I need snaps, paks and Wayland,\nthat won&apos;t run anyway\non my librebooted thinkpad\nturning glowies away\n\nIf you see use Ubuntu, I might say &quot;Hi&quot;,\nbut if you meet me running Arch, I&apos;m a talkative guy\nI&apos;ve been tryna fix my audio and solid state drive\nand I get a little closer every line I write\n\nAll these newgen Linux posers filling up my feed\nThey love proprietary software and KDE\nand the AUR maintainers&apos; tryna infect me\nGotta verify my age with systemD...\n\n•Site: https://denshi.org/","viewCount":569299,"lengthSeconds":98,"watchProgress":59.72443,"timeWatched":1792102725063,"isLive":false,"type":"video","_id":"XWa4BlA2HwFTOFHA","lastViewedPlaylistType":"","lastViewedPlaylistItemId":null}
{"videoId":"KW7hzWehuDo","title":"10 Things To Do After Installing openSUSE","author":"The Linux Cast","authorId":"UCylGUf9BvQooEFjgdNudoQg","published":1711587918000,"description":"Today I talk about 10 things you should do after you&apos;ve installed openSUSE. \n👇 PULL IT DOWN FOR THE GOOD STUFF 👇\n\nPatreon - https://patreon.com/thelinuxcast\nPaypal - https://paypal.me/thelinuxcast\nYoutube - https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCylGUf9BvQooEFjgdNudoQg/join\nKo-fi - https://ko-fi.com/thelinuxcast\n\n===== Follow us 🐧🐧 ======\nMERCH - https://shop.thelinuxcast.org/\nDiscord - https://discord.gg/62RPDBMH8W\nOdysee - https://odysee.com/$/invite/@thelinuxcast:4\nTILvids(Peertube) - https://tilvids.com/c/thelinuxcast_channel/videos\nMastodon- https://fosstodon.org/@thelinuxcast\nhttps://gitlab.com/thelinuxcast\nMatrix - https://matrix.to/#/<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/the\">#the</a>-linux-cast:matrix.org\nThe Website http://thelinuxcast.org/\nContact us email@thelinuxcast.org\nAmazon Wishlist - https://www.amazon.com/hz/wishlist/ls/1J3W9HF4O2M7T?ref_=wl_share\nLogo Courtesy of - pedropaulo.net\nIntro Courtesy of - https://www.fragcgi.com/?i=1\n\nSign up for encrypted email with Tutanota - https://mail.tutanota.com/signup?ref=RnNRMDFnZWY\n\n==== Special Thanks to Our Patrons! ====\nhttps://thelinuxcast.org/patrons/\n\n==== Referenced ====\nYaST Video - https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bQ6Z1OTC_G0\nBTRFS Video - https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FCgXYcIYDe0\nInstall flathub commands - https://flathub.org/setup/openSUSE\nOpenSUSE Forums - https://forums.opensuse.org/\nInstall Nvidia Drivers - https://github.com/pavinjosdev/zypperoni\n\n==== Time Stamps ====\n0:00 Intro\n0:43 A Couple Disclaimers\n1:38 Making Zypper Faster\n4:54 Learning YaST\n7:15 Create a Forum Account\n8:10 Get the Codecs\n11:12 Install Nvidia Drivers\n12:31 Get Familiar With Zypper\n16:10 Learn About BTRFS\n20:02 Install Flatpak\n20:48 Change Boot Delay\n22:00 Finally Updating Your System\n25:46 Wrapping Up\n\n<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/opensuse\">#opensuse</a>  <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/linux\">#linux</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/thelinuxcast\">#thelinuxcast</a>","viewCount":69304,"lengthSeconds":1662,"watchProgress":1391.713474,"timeWatched":1793122671653,"isLive":false,"type":"video","_id":"ZUvMEbQVShlhDOe0","lastViewedPlaylistType":"","lastViewedPlaylistItemId":null}
