{"videoId":"r5r4g3AL2as","title":"Ex-Google Officer: In 2 Years AI Will End Capitalism","author":"Neural Nutshell","authorId":"UCE0-acFJdnTPUCYlYoiq_fg","published":1788711307000,"description":"🔒 Make yourself and your family AI-scam proof, step by step → https://neuralnutshell.com/\n\nMo Mogodat, former Chief Business Officer at Google X, warns that artificial intelligence is about to replace all jobs, ending labor arbitrage and dismantling the foundational rule of capitalism as we know it. He states that without jobs, people will lose economic purchasing power, making it impossible to repay debts, and predicts the next 10 to 12 years will be unlike anything we’ve ever experienced. Mogodat argues that the economic system we were born into is already finished, and the next 15 years will bring a world that is unrecognizable. He explains that capitalism thrives on labor arbitrage, where workers are paid less than the value they create, but AI removes the worker from the equation entirely, breaking the system. He also discusses the unsustainability of universal basic income, the cycle of surveillance and control in Western societies, and how military spending could end world hunger if redirected.\n\n📚 Sources cited in this video:\n\nMo Gawdat, Official Website https://www.mogawdat.com/\n\nInternational Labour Organization, Generative AI and Jobs https://www.ilo.org/publications/generative-ai-jobs-global-analysis-potential-effects-job-quantity-and\n\nWorld Economic Forum, The Future of Jobs Report 2025 https://www.weforum.org/publications/the-future-of-jobs-report-2025/\n\nInternational Telecommunication Union, Mo Gawdat — AI for Good https://aiforgood.itu.int/speaker/mo-gawdat/\n\n\n⚠️ DISCLAIMER: This channel provides AI commentary and analysis\nfor educational and informational purposes only. Views expressed by\nguests are their own and do not represent the positions of\nany company or institution. We encourage viewers to consult\nmultiple sources and form their own conclusions.\n\n<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/ai\">#ai</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/agi\">#agi</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/artificialintelligence\">#artificialintelligence</a>","viewCount":523190,"lengthSeconds":950,"watchProgress":930.424094,"timeWatched":1791745157671,"isLive":false,"type":"video","_id":"zZ7Gs7GXLzF7oiHM","lastViewedPlaylistType":"","lastViewedPlaylistItemId":null}
{"videoId":"wU-4K3Yj5kY","title":"No Drama, Just Power. Why I Switched to openSUSE Tumbleweed.","author":"Gnu To Linux","authorId":"UC95zeRjDuxifm06s1BJeuZg","published":1771536882000,"description":"After 15 years of jumping between Linux distributions, I finally found the one that checks every box. In this video, I’m diving into why openSUSE Tumbleweed has become my daily driver.\n\nWe look at the incredible power of YaST, the &quot;safety net&quot; of Snapper (built-in system rollbacks from the boot menu!), and why I’ve moved away from American-based distros in favor of this European-engineered powerhouse. If you want a rolling release that doesn&apos;t break and gives you total control, this is it.\n\nHead to https://gnutolinux.com/ for tools and tips for all new Linux users including:\nDistro Finder\nopenSUSE user guide\n\nWhat we cover:\n\nWhy the &quot;German Tank&quot; (openSUSE) is so stable.\n\nSnapper: How to never fear an update again.\n\nYaST: The tool I wish every Linux distro had.\n\nKDE Plasma 6.6: Blazing fast updates on Tumbleweed.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/@openSUSE","viewCount":43312,"lengthSeconds":269,"watchProgress":62.71744,"timeWatched":1793121477238,"isLive":false,"type":"video","_id":"zkBCmI1AfHooxADt","lastViewedPlaylistType":"","lastViewedPlaylistItemId":null}
